Package: thunderbird-closetobackground
Version: @DEBIAN_VERSION@
Section: mail
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0, gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0
Suggests: thunderbird (>= 128), gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
@HOMEPAGE@Description: Thunderbird close-to-tray helper and add-on for Linux
 Keep Thunderbird running in the system tray with unread badges and
 new-mail notifications. Supports GNOME with an AppIndicator extension,
 including native Wayland sessions, and other StatusNotifierItem hosts.
 .
 This package installs the native helper and configures Thunderbird to
 install/update the bundled add-on automatically on its next start.
 Users can disable the add-on. Existing unrelated policies are preserved.
 It does not edit user profiles or enable GNOME extensions automatically.
 .
 Native Thunderbird 128 through 153 is required. Flatpak and Snap builds
 are not supported. On Wayland, use Thunderbird's own minimize button;
 compositor-only minimize shortcuts keep their usual behavior.
